course: dictionary
lesson: 7354
title: Playful words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Playful means full of fun and wanting to play. A puppy that chases its own tail is playful. When you meet this word, look at the words around it. Fun, games and jokes are clues.
explain: Playful can also describe a remark or an action. It is meant as a joke and not seriously. «"Hacker" once meant a clever, playful programmer», which means someone who enjoyed clever tricks with computers, not someone doing harm.
explain: Playful does not always mean safe. A playful dog can still jump up or nip, so ask its owner first. To check your meaning, swap in "full of fun" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Playful means full of fun and wanting to play.
fact: A playful remark or action is meant as a joke, not seriously.
fact: The adverb is playfully, and the noun is playfulness.
fact: «The bee's knees» and «the cat's pyjamas» were playful nonsense in 1920s American slang, meaning something excellent.
fact: «Coucou!» is a warm, playful hi for family, small children and good friends.
exercise: «The puppy gave a playful push with its nose.» What does playful mean here? | Very tired and sleepy | Angry and shouting | Lost and afraid | *Full of fun, wanting to play
exercise: Which word is closest in meaning to playful? | Silent | *Full of fun | Cross | Tired
exercise: Ella's dad made a playful remark about her messy room. What was it meant to be? | *A joke, meant to be fun | A serious order to tidy up now | A warning about danger | A rule about bedtime
test: Which word is the adverb of playful? | Playful, but more playful | *Playfully | Playfulness | Plays
test: In a story, a character gives a playful smile. What mood does the reader know about? | Bored and tired | Angry and cross | *Happy and joking | Frightened of the dark
exam: Why should you ask the owner before patting a playful dog? | Playful dogs are always sad | *A playful dog can still jump up or nip | Because dogs cannot be patted | Because owners are always cross
